  "comparison": "subset",
  "notes": "watch-publication-disposition inputs are request_started (boolean), attempts (nonnegative integer), http_response_on_every_attempt (boolean), succeeded (boolean), and restart_with_sending (boolean). First match wins: restart_with_sending -> unconfirmed; succeeded -> processed; request_started and http_response_on_every_attempt -> released; other request_started -> unconfirmed; otherwise released. A surviving sending record overrides all runtime fields. Production proves response coverage using answeredAttempts == attempts with attempts > 0; the final HTTP status alone is insufficient. An acknowledged failure is not retried in the current session but remains discoverable in a later session. Unsent work stays discoverable under existing Start/Stop behavior. processed and unconfirmed hold the watch key against automatic publication; an explicit Upload file command is independent of that hold. watch-retain inputs are keys (array of checkpoint key strings), files (array of {key, parent_exists, fingerprint}, with fingerprint string or null), and optional sending_keys (array of keys, default empty). The keys include processed, unconfirmed and sending records. A sending key is always kept. Otherwise a key is kept when its parent is missing or the current fingerprint equals the key. fingerprint is the current complete key returned by the platform fingerprint helper; null means no current fingerprint. Output kept preserves input keys order. The adapter supplies observations to the same pure retain helper used by production; it does not implement the retention decision itself.",
  "requirement_ids": [
    "CORE-025"
  ],
